cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "@micropasts/glb-model-viewer"
message: "If you use this software in your research, museum exhibition, or digital heritage project, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pett
    given-names: Daniel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0246-2335"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MicroPasts/glb-viewer"
url: "https://github.com/MicroPasts/glb-viewer"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight, high-precision Three.js GLB/glTF 3D artifact and model viewer
  for React, built for cultural heritage, numismatics, archaeology, and
  scientific inspection. Features 3-tier physical scale calibration, a
  collapsible zebra photoscale bar with reference object silhouettes, portable
  W3C/IIIF 3D spatial annotations with guided tours, BVH-accelerated surface
  measurements, paradata records, glTF animation playback, cross-section
  slicing, diagnostic shading, and multi-format mesh exports.
keywords:
  - 3d-viewer
  - gltf
  - glb
  - threejs
  - react
  - cultural-heritage
  - archaeology
  - numismatics
  - iiif
  - paradata
  - photogrammetry
